---
// Every statement here traces to the facts inventory in lib/legal.js.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../lib/legal.js';
import { EXAMS } from '../lib/exams.js';
import { authEnabled } from '../lib/accounts/config.js';

const mail = `mailto:${LEGAL.email}`;
// The same credit the footer prints.
const sources = EXAMS.map((e) => `${e.source}, ${e.corpus.minYear}–${e.corpus.maxYear}`).join('; ');
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The rules for using SawaalBox: the free beta, accounts, fair use, how far to trust the answers, and the law that applies."
  heading="Terms of use"
  standfirst="The rules for using SawaalBox, in plain words."
  numbered={true}
>
  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="about">
    <h2 id="about">About SawaalBox</h2>
    <p>
      SawaalBox is a website of past questions from Indian competitive exams, starting with the UPSC Civil Services
      Preliminary Examination. You can read and search them without an account, and mark questions and keep revision
      lists. It is run by {LEGAL.operator}, {LEGAL.place} ("we"). SawaalBox is not connected with UPSC or any government
      body.
    </p>
    <p>By using SawaalBox you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use it.</p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="beta">
    <h2 id="beta">The beta</h2>
    <p>SawaalBox is in beta. {LEGAL.betaTerms}</p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="accounts">
    <h2 id="accounts">Your account</h2>
    {
      !authEnabled && (
        <p class="legal-aside">Sign-in is not open yet. This section applies once it is.</p>
      )
    }
    <ul>
      <li>Accounts are for people aged {LEGAL.minAge} or over. Reading and searching need no account, so they are open to everyone.</li>
      <li>You sign in with your own Google account. An account is for one person; please don't share it.</li>
      <li>Keep your Google account secure: anyone who can sign in to it can use your SawaalBox account.</li>
      <li>
        You can ask us to delete your account at any time by emailing <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.email}</a>. Your marks and lists
        are deleted with it.
      </li>
      <li>We may suspend or delete an account that breaks these terms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>How we handle your account's data is set out in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="fair-use">
    <h2 id="fair-use">Using SawaalBox fairly</h2>
    <p>Use SawaalBox for your own study. Please don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        scrape the site or the search service, or send them automated or bulk requests. The search service runs on a small
        server, and heavy use slows it down for everyone;
      </li>
      <li>try to get into anyone else's account or data, or get around the site's security;</li>
      <li>try to overload, break or disrupt the site;</li>
      <li>use SawaalBox for anything unlawful.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="content">
    <h2 id="content">Questions and answers</h2>
    <p>Questions are reproduced from past papers: {sources}.</p>
    <p>
      The questions, answers, subjects, topics and difficulty levels were taken from a compilation of past papers.
      Mistakes can creep in, in the compilation or in how we copied it, and no subject expert has checked them. Questions
      that UPSC cancelled, and answers that are disputed, are flagged where we know of it. Always check an
      answer against official sources, such as the answer keys UPSC publishes, before you rely on it. If you find a
      mistake, please <a href="/contact">tell us</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Search finds questions by what they are about, so its results are a guide: it can miss a relevant question or show
      one that is not.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="no-promise">
    <h2 id="no-promise">No guarantees</h2>
    <p>
      SawaalBox is provided as it is. We don't promise that it is complete, correct, or always available. The search
      service can take up to a minute to start after a quiet spell, and may sometimes be unavailable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="liability">
    <h2 id="liability">Limits on our responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      As far as the law allows, we are not responsible for any loss that comes from using SawaalBox or relying on it: for
      example, a wrong answer, a question the search missed, or marks and lists that are lost. Nothing in these terms
      limits a responsibility that Indian law does not allow to be limited.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="changes">
    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may change, pause or stop parts of SawaalBox. When we change these terms, we update the date at the top; if a
      change affects what you can do with your account, we will say so on the site before it takes effect. You can stop
      using SawaalBox at any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="law">
    <h2 id="law">Law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at {LEGAL.place} have jurisdiction over any dispute
      about them. If something goes wrong, please write to us first at <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.email}</a>; most problems are
      quicker to sort out that way.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section data-numbered aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms go to <a href={mail}>{LEGAL.email}</a>. The <a href="/contact">contact page</a> says what
      to include and when to expect a reply.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
